{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790959981,"nonce":"1oombcGCUjIQ4UBV2l3WtyzCop8=","title":"A Haxe throw symbolises its whole stack with dladdr","message":"Measured 2026-10-02 on the gpu plugin fixture (debug, hybrid): 23–39 ms of about 380 main-thread samples are `hlp_throw` → `ash_std::error::throw_impl` → `capture_exception_stack` → `HLInterpreter::prepare_call_stack` → `trace_sites` → `dladdr`, for the handful of expected errors the fixture's `refused(...)` checks raise through caribou imports.\n\n`dladdr` searches the image's exported symbols, and caribou's binaries export every symbol (`-export_dynamic`, needed for hatch plugins), so each frame is a search of a large table. Capturing return addresses at the throw and symbolising when the stack is read (`CallStack.exceptionStack()`, an uncaught error's report) would make a caught error cost what a throw costs.\n\nAsh owns the capture; this records what it costs a hosted program.","files":null}]}